From: Jay Hemnani <193022578+jayhemnani9910@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:19:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] 09977: Apply R_X86_64_PC64 ELF relocations

The x86-64 handler had no case for R_X86_64_PC64 (S + A - P, 64-bit),
so these relocations were left unapplied and reported as unhandled. A
Linux kernel module uses one per __jump_table entry for the static key
field, e.g. 66 in 9p.ko.
---
 .../format/elf/relocation/X86_64_ElfRelocationHandler.java    | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Ghidra/Processors/x86/src/main/java/ghidra/app/util/bin/format/elf/relocation/X86_64_ElfRelocationHandler.java b/Ghidra/Processors/x86/src/main/java/ghidra/app/util/bin/format/elf/relocation/X86_64_ElfRelocationHandler.java
index 993bfbf700..1cdbc19b71 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Processors/x86/src/main/java/ghidra/app/util/bin/format/elf/relocation/X86_64_ElfRelocationHandler.java
+++ b/Ghidra/Processors/x86/src/main/java/ghidra/app/util/bin/format/elf/relocation/X86_64_ElfRelocationHandler.java
@@ -137,6 +137,10 @@ public class X86_64_ElfRelocationHandler extends
 				memory.setByte(relocationAddress, (byte) value);
 				byteLength = 1;
 				break;
+			case R_X86_64_PC64:
+				value = symbolValue + addend - offset;
+				memory.setLong(relocationAddress, value);
+				break;
 			case R_X86_64_PC32:
 				value = symbolValue + addend - offset;
 				value = value & 0xffffffff;
-- 
